[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\fill[gray!35] (-1.1,0) -- plot[domain=-2:7,smooth,variable=\x] ({0.55*\x},{1.4+0.18*\x-0.012*\x*\x}) -- (3.85,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-2.0,0) -- (4.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.6) -- (0,3.3) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,domain=-2.6:7.6,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({0.55*\x},{1.4+0.18*\x-0.012*\x*\x});
\draw (-1.1,0.12) -- (-1.1,-0.12) node[below] {$-2$};
\draw (3.85,0.12) -- (3.85,-0.12) node[below] {$7$};
\node at (2.4,2.9) {$y=f(x)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The shaded region is divided into $6$ strips of equal width so that $\int_{-2}^{7}f(x)\,dx$ can be estimated by the Trapezoidal rule. What is the strip width $h$?

